{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Then Moses called for all the elders of Israel.</b> And although HaShem said to him, ״Speak to all the congregation of Israel,״ its meaning would be as the verse says (Leviticus 4:13): ״If the whole congregation of Israel errs,״ which is said of the elders, as is explained in its place (Torat Kohanim), ״and he said to them״ refers to the rest of the people, according to the rule of all the commandments of HaShem to Israel, which were transmitted through Moses (Eruvin 54a)." "<b>Or</b> it is possible that he spoke only to the elders, and they would speak to all the congregation of Israel; and this commandment differs from the rest of the commandments in the Torah because Israel had not yet entered the covenant and were not trained to enter into observance and practice. Therefore he would speak to the elders, and each elder would speak gently and in a manner acceptable to the members of his family, so that they would be willing to do it."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:05.793229114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}